Look at these three lines in the RunCommand:

double error = targetHeading - heading;

while (error > 180) error -= 360;
while (error < -180) error += 360;

Error is how far off we are. Positive error means turn right, negative means turn left.

But heading wraps around at +/-180. If the robot faces 170 and the target is -170, the real error is 20 degrees — not 340.

The while loops wrap error into [-180, 180]. This guarantees the robot always takes the shortest turn.

Without wrapping, the robot would spin 340 degrees to reach a target 20 degrees away.
